sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Next.js Client
    participant AuthCtrl as AuthController
    participant SecFilter as JwtAuthenticationFilter
    participant AuthService as AuthService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (users, auth_sessions)

    Note over Client,DB: User Login Flow
    Client->>AuthCtrl: POST /api/v1/auth/login {email, password}
    AuthCtrl->>AuthService: authenticate(email, password)
    AuthService->>DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?
    AuthService->>AuthService: Verify BCrypt hash (Strength: 12)
    AuthService->>AuthService: Generate JWT Access Token (15m expiry)
    AuthService->>AuthService: Generate Opaque Refresh Token + Family ID
    AuthService->>DB: INSERT INTO auth_sessions (user_id, token_hash=SHA256(rt), token_family_id, expires_at=NOW()+7d)
    AuthService-->>Client: Set-Cookie: accessToken (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite) & Set-Cookie: refreshToken (HttpOnly) + CSRF Header

    Note over Client,DB: Authenticated API Request
    Client->>SecFilter: GET /api/v1/emails (with Cookie: accessToken)
    SecFilter->>SecFilter: Validate JWT signature & expiry (HMAC-SHA256)
    SecFilter->>SecFilter: Extract UserPrincipal (userId, email)
    SecFilter->>Client: Pass to Controller with SecurityContext populated

    Note over Client,DB: Token Refresh Flow with Rotation & Reuse Detection
    Client->>AuthCtrl: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh (Cookie: refreshToken)
    AuthCtrl->>AuthService: rotateRefreshToken(rawRefreshToken)
    AuthService->>AuthService: Compute SHA256(rawRefreshToken)
    AuthService->>DB: SELECT * FROM auth_sessions WHERE token_hash = ?
    alt Token already revoked (Token Reuse Detected!)
        AuthService->>DB: UPDATE auth_sessions SET revoked_at=NOW() WHERE token_family_id = ?
        AuthService-->>Client: 401 Unauthorized (Security alert: token reuse detected, all sessions revoked)
    else Token valid & active
        AuthService->>DB: UPDATE auth_sessions SET revoked_at=NOW(), replaced_by_token_id=new_session_id
        AuthService->>AuthService: Generate new Access Token + new Refresh Token (same family)
        AuthService->>DB: INSERT INTO auth_sessions (new_session_id, token_hash=SHA256(new_rt), family_id)
        AuthService-->>Client: Set-Cookie: new accessToken & new refreshToken
    end

    Note over Client,DB: Logout Flow
    Client->>AuthCtrl: POST /api/v1/auth/logout
    AuthCtrl->>AuthService: revokeSession(refreshToken)
    AuthService->>DB: UPDATE auth_sessions SET revoked_at=NOW() WHERE token_hash = SHA256(rt)
    AuthCtrl-->>Client: Clear cookies (accessToken, refreshToken)

